e (. or x knocks too);  runs of 2-9 repeats -> multitap (44 33 555); 2-9 singles -> T9\n [0-9a-f] even, x2 ................ hex (D3); c1-e9/81-a9 + 40 -> EBCDIC cp037\n hex x4 starting fffe (D19 LE 4e00) / feff (D20 BE 004e), 00 every 2nd byte = UTF-16: .decode('utf-16') takes EITHER BOM;\n   fffe0000/0000feff -> UTF-32; NULs in a non-LE/BE 4-byte pattern -> middle-endian; d8xx dcxx -> surrogates, then NFKC;\n   pairs/quads swapped -> byte-swap words; base64 with AG/AA rhythm -> b64 then utf-16-le; LSB-first bits\n . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n a/b in 5s ....... Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> 0-15 = HEX nibbles); up to 25 -> letters; odd casing -> Bacon via case\n ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17);\n   unknown 16 tokens -> map them by the crib hex `4e 69 63 65 20 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads/#RRGGBB/4e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+004E U+0069 (D25, 7 B/char) / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX / \\u{4E} -> chr(int(h,16)); mixed prefixes -> one alternation tokenizer\n   LATIN SMALL LETTER I / \\N{..} -> unicodedata.lookup;  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n N:c,N:c, ... digits:payload, ..... NETSTRINGS (D24, every len 1): count-cursor parse, never split(','); payload `,`/`:`\n   are data (1:,, 1::,). No comma -> bencode (l..e, i..e)/sexp; tag ,#!~^]} -> tnetstring; $len CRLF -> RESP; hex len -> chunked\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = -> base64url (D11); [0-9A-Za-z] -> base62 (x1.34)/base36 (x1.55); no 0OIl+/= -> base58; 0-9A-Z $%*+-./: -> base45\n <~ ... ~> around ! .. u ......... ASCII85 (D23): a85decode(t,adobe=True); no <~ -> a85decode (z = 4 NULs);\n   RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> b85decode; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85; xbtoa Begin -> btoa\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92;  no chunk structure -> bignum radix\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA;  ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C G T only -> DNA 2-bit / codon\nNON-ASCII: ⠝⠊⠉⠑ -> Braille (⠼ = number sign); fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ -> NFKC;  ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ -> upside-down (from_upside_down, maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx + spaces -> ROT8000; dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048; emoji 1/byte -> base100; CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n zero-width U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> bits; U+E00xx tags -> cp-0xE0000; FE00../E0100.. selectors -> bytes; one block with\n   ord-ord(crib) constant -> code-point offset; runes/Greek/Cyrillic, lengths kept -> crib map; Cyrillic look-alikes -> homoglyph\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English -> Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also +5 -> ROT18/ROT5;  mirror a<->z -> Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic -> Beaufort (primer then plaintext -> autokey);  crib map consistent, not affine -> keyword subst\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3 = prompt number):\n w.rail_solve | redefence | w.col_solve | route/Caesar box | skip k | riffle | word order; spaces are ciphertext; START `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Pun -> key (D18 \"Three rails\"); \"Same/Another\" = 1 knob\nPROGRAMS (\"language\", D26-27): + - . runs = Brainfuck (w.bf_dec; running sum at `.`; step cap, NEVER node/eval)\n Ook. Ook! pairs (D27, prompt QUOTES the tokens) / Blub. / MoO / pi ka -> w.bfd_dec (pair from token 0; `Ook! Ook.` = OUTPUT)\n unknown/emoji/unspaced tokens -> crib-assign to +-<>[].,; ()[]{}<> only -> Brain-Flak; lines of `chicken` -> Chicken\n i d s o -> Deadfish; only space/TAB/LF pushes -> Whitespace; \"..\",@ v>^ -> Befunge; output not English -> decode it AGAIN\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18: 6-8 char rail-3 slug tail);\n lines 19/20 own BOM, 21/22 gzip/zlib, 23 `<~..~>`, 24 `1:c,`, 25 `U+XXXX`, 26 BF / 27 Ook from cell 0. NEVER pre-decode\n a line (D23, D25: all NN wrong); register_free(name, TODAY'S DAY, fn) on the RAW line -- a DAYS entry must round-trip\n the GM bytes: use lib's encoder (bf_enc, bfd_enc(s,\"ook\")), never an ad-hoc one (D26 60 s kill, D27 34.9 s).\n STACKS (D16-17, D19-21): output hex/digits/b32/a-p/NUL-rhythm/compressed-magic bytes -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-bf-line-26\", \"concept\": \"carried solver: Mastery esolang lines (26 BF, 27 Ook) must be routed by a GM-faithful encoder or a decode-only registration\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the solver's runtime DAYS[26] encoder ('+'*ord per cell + '.>') did not reproduce the GM's one-cell signed-delta bytes -> line 26 never round-tripped -> 64