take EXACTLY `len` chars, require `,` (or end) right after, advance; accept only if the WHOLE text\n100\t  parses (else None, so plain text never matches); `register_free(\"netstr\", 24, fn)` for the Mastery line. Never\n101\t  `split(',')`. The loop already covers len > 1 and mixed lengths; unbuilt knobs: len in UTF-8 BYTES vs chars,\n102\t  hex/varint/binary length prefixes, tnetstrings (type tag `,#^!~]}` instead of `,`), bencode (`4:spam`, `l..e`),\n103\t  RESP (`$5\\r\\nhello\\r\\n`), HTTP chunked, `index:char` frames OUT OF ORDER, `count:char` run-length, nested frames.\n104\t- **Esoteric program + its SPELLING (D26-D27)** -- the blob is a PROGRAM; its output is the text. The program never\n105\t  changed: ONE cell from 0, each char = a run of ONLY `+` or ONLY `-` equal to the delta from the previous char, then\n106\t  `.`; no loops/`<>`/`,`, never wraps, no newline. What changed is the token spelling. Values seen: D26 raw Brainfuck\n107\t  `+ - .` (3406 B for 109 chars, ~31 B/char; Mastery line 26 = 166-217 B); D27 Ook! words `Ook.`/`Ook!` joined by ONE\n108\t  space, PAIRED from token 0, only three pairs (`Ook. Ook.` +, `Ook! Ook!` -, `Ook! Ook.` .), NO `Ook?` at all, ~314\n109\t  B/char (33929 B single / 34569 B TT); Mastery line 27 = the same over a 4-5 char tail (1672-2172 B), restarting at\n110\t  cell 0, 133/133 sets. Parse rule: tokenize the whole text into the dialect's tokens (Ook: `(?i)Ook\\s*([.?!])`; the\n111\t  text minus tokens/whitespace must be empty, even count), map PAIRS to BF (`.?` > `?.` < `..` + `!!` - `!.` . `.!` ,\n112\t  `!?` [ `?!` ]), then the step-capped `_bf` interpreter (8-bit cells, `,` = 0), printable + slug gate. lib:\n113\t  `warmups_codecs.bf_dec` (raw BF) and `bfd_dec` (Ook/Blub/short Ook/COW/Pikalang/Alphuck/ReverseFuck/Binaryfuck +\n114\t  crib-solved unknown <= 8-token map); their encoders `bf_enc` / `bfd_enc(s, \"ook\")` reproduce the GM's DELTA bytes.\n115\t- **Line wrapper / positional routing** -- `NN<TAB>fragment` n