{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AHAeYadoNZ2XDVQwZX1QrV","type":"tool_result","content":"28\t  D27 a knob with NO \"Same\"/\"Another\" cue: the prompt QUOTED the dialect's own tokens; D28 left the esolangs for a\n29\t  COMPOSITION of two day-3/day-12 codecs, the prompt re-using D3's \"sixteen-fingered friend\" verbatim. On an unknown\n30\t  shape read the blob's STRUCTURE (repeating unit, token shape, a tiny alphabet of operators/words) and name the spec\n31\t  from it + the pun; a prompt that QUOTES an old day's riddle = that day's codec is one of the layers.\n32\t- Mastery is cumulative: day N = 5N-2 sets x N numbered lines `NN<TAB>fragment`, line k = day k's encoding (D26 line =\n33\t  a 166-217 B BF program printing a 5-char tail; D27 line = 1672-2172 B of Ook printing a 4-5 char tail; D28 line = 8\n34\t  (136/138) or 10 reversed-hex chars = a 4-5 char tail; 138 x 28).\n35\t  Last line has no trailing newline; fragments split mid-word and join verbatim.\n36\t- Clocks: D1-D15 TT ~5-8 s / Mastery ~5-9 s windows; since D16 mostly `deadline: null` (D18: 30 s / 105 s). The HARNESS\n37\t  kills solve.py at 60 s regardless (D17, D21). D23 and D25 Mastery first submit INCORRECT (all NN wrong, pre-decoded\n38\t  line), fixed on the SAME attempt; D26 Mastery 128 x 26 solve 64.9 s, 0 answers (harness kill; a live worker\n39\t  hand-decoded, CORRECT ~2 min 20 s). D27 TT 4.4 s (solve 0.53 s), Mastery 133 x 27 38.2 s (solve 34.9 s -- the same\n40\t  bad-encoder routing as D26 on line 27, survived only because lib's DAYS[26] had been fixed overnight), both first try.\n41\t  D28 TT 5.1 s (solve 1.05 s), Mastery 138 x 28 9.3 s (solve 6.2 s), both first try, no DAYS[28] registered.\n42\t\n43\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8f20a12-b094-46cb-8e63-cbcb2408e4ba","uuid":"e518d896-914d-4ab5-a68b-278c1b2bf07b","timestamp"