{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013RFSD8PAg3ra77LQxnxixx","type":"tool_result","content":"198\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n199\t- DELIVERY: Mastery = ONE zip saved as `blob-01.txt` (check magic, not extension); read member `blob-0N.txt`, never the\n200\t  bundle (D7: a slug that is a word suffix `py-...` is the tell). Missing set bytes = a downloader problem (D1, ~12 fails),\n201\t  not a solver one. Dry runs on renamed per-set copies do NOT reproduce the real layout: test on the raw delivery.\n202\t- NEVER REPLACE THE LANE SOLVER (D21): copy the previous day's warmups `solve.py` and add the new codec as ONE branch\n203\t  (whole-blob step + `register_free(name, day, fn)`). A fresh generic brute-force solver passes single/TT (one short\n204\t  blob) and then dies at 60 s on Mastery (103 sets x 21 lines). A prebuilt lib codec is equally useless if the carried\n205\t  solver never routes to it (D18 `rail_solve`). First move on a new day: lib's whole-blob candidates (`decode_chunk` +\n206\t  `warmups_codecs.CANDIDATES`/`*_solve`).\n207\t- CHEAP PATH FIRST, RETURN EARLY (D17): return the first candidate that yields a full slug; call the joint ranker only on\n208\t  a miss (83 x 17 passed 60 s when every set paid the joint search; a per-set `peel` BFS blew a 30 s window on D12). Time\n209\t  the real Mastery case (`hctf solver-test`) after every new codec; profile `answer()` per set when solve passes ~5 s.\n210\t- PRE-DECODING MASTERY LINES (D23 113/113 and D25 123/123 sets wrong once each): never rewrite a numbered line in place to plaintext before\n211\t  `decode_chunked`/`_joint_free` -- the joint search has no \"identity\" choice, so a plain line gets a leftover free codec\n212\t  (digit ROT5 turned `el-46` into `el-91`). Register the codec instead and let it claim the RAW line. Check the joined\n213\t  Mastery sentence of one set by eye before a timed start; all-sets-wrong-in-the-same-field = one line's routing.\n214\t  D25: a day with NO registered codec makes `_positional` send its (pre-decoded, plain) line to `_unknown_line_cands`,\n215\t  which mangles it -- register the codec for today's day number even if the whole-blob path already decodes it.\n216\t  D26: a REGISTERED `DAYS` codec whose encoder doesn't round-trip the GM bytes is as bad as none (and slower: every set\n217\t  pays the unknown-line + joint search -> 60 s kill). D27 repeated it with an Ook encoder (34.9 s, survived). Many-to-one\n218\t  codecs (programs, padding, case-free, whitespace variants) can't be round-tripped -> use `register_free`\n219\t  (decode-only) or lib's GM-faithful encoder (`bf_enc`, `bfd_enc`). D28 passed with NO day-28 codec only because line\n220\t  28 was the LAST line (unknown-last-line path); the next day it is a middle line -> register `(28, \"revhex\",\n221\t  lambda s: s.encode().hex()[::-1], lambda t: bytes.fromhex(t[::-1]).decode(), False)` before the timed runs.\n222\t- ENGLISH SCORING: don't count single letters/hex reads as English (D3 timeout); a rot-N must beat the unshifted text by a\n223\t  margin (D4). Rot-N is `decode_chunk`'s catch-all, so ANY unknown plain transform comes back as plausible rot garbage\n224\t  (D12 reversal `69-fove-n`, D13's rejected `ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31` = rot-N of Atbash): gibberish slug words = an unknown\n225\t  transform, not a GM quirk. Several free transforms in one blob (rot13/rev/Atbash/Caesar/ROT47) -> decide JOINTLY, each\n226\t  once (`_joint_free`), rank full 3-word slugs first (D14 set22); prune by alphabet before the joint search (D15).\n227\t- REVERSAL GRANULARITY (D28): a reversed STRICT string is still in the strict charset, so it \"decodes\" to junk instead of"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8f20a12-b094-46cb-8e63-cbcb2408e4ba","uuid":"1eb9cb54-5cbc-4a2d-a91d-bae327420364","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:10:42.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/warmups.md","content":"## Pitfalls that cost time\n- DELIVERY: Mastery = ONE zip saved as `blob-01.txt` (check magic, not extension); read member `blob-0N.txt`, never the\n  bundle (D7: a slug that is a word suffix `py-...` is the tell). Missing set bytes = a downloader problem (D1, ~12 fails),\n  not a solver one. Dry runs on renamed per-set copies do NOT reproduce the real layout: test on the raw delivery.\n- NEVER REPLACE THE LANE SOLVER (D21): copy the previous day's warmups `solve.py` and add the new codec as ONE branch\n  (whole-blob step + `register_free(name, day, fn)`). A fresh generic brute-force solver passes single/TT (one short\n  blob) and then dies at 60 s on Mastery (103 sets x 21 lines). A prebuilt lib codec is equally useless if the carried\n  solver never routes to it (D18 `rail_solve`). First move on a new day: lib's whole-blob candidates (`decode_chunk` +\n  `warmups_codecs.CANDIDATES`/`*_solve`).\n- CHEAP PATH FIRST, RETURN EARLY (D17): return the first candidate that yields a full slug; call the joint ranker only on\n  a miss (83 x 17 passed 60 s when every set paid the joint search; a per-set `peel` BFS blew a 30 s window on D12). Time\n  the real Mastery case (`hctf solver-test`) after every new codec; profile `answer()` per set when solve passes ~5 s.\n- PRE-DECODING MASTERY LINES (D23 113/113 and D25 123/123 sets wrong once each): never rewrite a numbered line in place to plaintext before\n  `decode_chunked`/`_joint_free` -- the joint search has no \"identity\" choice, so a plain line gets a leftover free codec\n  (digit ROT5 turned `el-46` into `el-91`). Register the codec instead and let it claim the RAW line. Check the joined\n  Mastery sentence of one set by eye before a timed start; all-sets-wrong-in-the-same-field = one line's routing.\n  D25: a day with NO registered codec makes `_positional` send its (pre-decoded, plain) line to `_unknown_line_cands`,\n  which mangles it -- register the codec for today's day number even if the whole-blob path already decodes it.\n  D26: a REGISTERED `DAYS` codec whose encoder doesn't round-trip the GM bytes is as bad as none (and slower: every set\n  pays the unknown-line + joint search -> 60 s kill). D27 repeated it with an Ook encoder (34.9 s, survived). Many-to-one\n  codecs (programs, padding, case-free, whitespace variants) can't be round-tripped -> use `register_free`\n  (decode-only) or lib's GM-faithful encoder (`bf_enc`, `bfd_enc`). D28 passed with NO day-28 codec only because line\n  28 was the LAST line (unknown-last-line path); the next day it is a middle line -> register `(28, \"revhex\",\n  lambda s: s.encode().hex()[::-1], lambda t: bytes.fromhex(t[::-1]).decode(), False)` before the timed runs.\n- ENGLISH SCORING: don't count single letters/hex reads as English (D3 timeout); a rot-N must beat the unshifted text by a\n  margin (D4). Rot-N is `decode_chunk`'s catch-all, so ANY unknown plain transform comes back as plausible rot garbage\n  (D12 reversal `69-fove-n`, D13's rejected `ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31` = rot-N of Atbash): gibberish slug words = an unknown\n  transform, not a GM quirk. Several free transforms in one blob (rot13/rev/Atbash/Caesar/ROT47) -> decide JOINTLY, each\n  once (`_joint_free`), rank full 3-word slugs first (D14 set22); prune by alphabet before the joint search (D15).\n- REVERSAL GRANULARITY (D28): a reversed STRICT string is still in the strict charset, so it \"decodes\" to junk instead of","numLines":30,"startLine":198,"totalLines":262}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013RFSD8PAg3ra77LQxnxixx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
